{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_5147e0f84dc3630f4b4baf5e94324e30bdba9f738e5ff39756f237390b08108b", "title": "The Legend of Sleepy Hollow", "text": "\"The Legend of Sleepy Hollow\" is a short story of speculative fiction by American author Washington Irving, contained in his collection of 34 essays and short stories entitled, \"The Sketch Book of Geoffrey Crayon, Gent. \". Written while Irving was living abroad in Birmingham, England, \"The Legend of Sleepy Hollow\" was first published in 1820. Along with Irving's companion piece \"Rip Van Winkle\", \"The Legend of Sleepy Hollow\" is among the earliest examples of American fiction with enduring popularity, especially during Halloween because of a character known as the headless horseman believed to be a Hessian soldier who lost his head to a cannonball in battle.", "score": 36.6512}, {"id": "hp_doc_b527eaf68035ed810041ec7cf4602a80d44a9d2e258f63f87f4f235d6f80d722", "title": "Ichabod Crane", "text": "Ichabod Crane is a fictional character and the protagonist in Washington Irving's short story, \"The Legend of Sleepy Hollow\", first published in 1820.", "score": 33.868}, {"id": "hp_doc_d9d8c8a27e4c3dbd13d4eaaa0ff6d803c6d8992b6b1e553210eb421b6454aa2e", "title": "Headless Horseman (Legend of Sleepy Hollow)", "text": "The Headless Horseman is a fictional character from the short story \"The Legend of Sleepy Hollow\" by American author Washington Irving. The story, from Irving's collection of short stories entitled \"The Sketch Book of Geoffrey Crayon, Gent. \", has worked itself into known American folklore/legend through literature and film. It is generally about a Headless Horseman.", "score": 30.6754}], "remaining_searches": 2}
